\description{
Fits one ellipsoid to each group of points and draws it as a solid with
\code{\link[=geom_ellipsoid_3d]{geom_ellipsoid_3d()}}: the three-dimensional counterpart of
\code{\link[ggplot2:stat_ellipse]{ggplot2::stat_ellipse()}}, whose \code{type} and \code{level} it takes over. The
ellipsoid is the unit sphere carried through the square root of a shape
matrix S onto the set of points p with (p - centre)' S^-1 (p - centre) <= 1,
computed in the scale-transformed units of the position axes.
}
\details{
\code{type} chooses the centre and the scatter matrix V:
\itemize{
\item \code{"t"} (the default) the location and scatter of a multivariate t
distribution with five degrees of freedom, fitted by iterative
reweighting as \code{MASS::cov.trob()} does, which keeps outlying points from
inflating the ellipsoid;
\item \code{"norm"} the mean and the sample covariance;
\item \code{"euclid"} the mean and a sphere of radius \code{level}, in data units.
}

\code{kind} chooses what the ellipsoid covers, with p = 3 dimensions and n
points in the group:
\itemize{
\item \code{"data"} (the default) the spread of the observations, S = r^2 V with
r^2 = p F(level; p, n - 1), the scaling of \code{\link[ggplot2:stat_ellipse]{ggplot2::stat_ellipse()}};
\item \code{"se"} the confidence region of the centre, S = r^2 V / n with
r^2 = p (n - 1) / (n - p) F(level; p, n - p), Hotelling's T^2 region
for the mean of a normal sample. \code{vegan3d::orglellipse(kind = "se")}
draws the same shape V / n scaled by a chi-square quantile, the
large-sample limit of r^2;
\item \code{"ehull"} the smallest ellipsoid that contains every point of the group,
as \code{vegan3d::orglellipse(kind = "ehull")}, computed by Khachiyan's
algorithm; \code{type} and \code{level} are not used.
}

A group needs at least four points that do not lie on one plane; other
groups are dropped with a message.
